  nonce: 6a0c  # 6a0c
  message: "PROGRESS 2026-09-26: RUST, SWIFT, KOTLIN, SCALA DONE in PR #1235 (merged). Remaining: java, c, cpp, csharp (+ WI-dokib, elixir's twin). Status stays violated.\n\nTwo shared helpers in analyze/base.py now carry the rule for every analyzer that adopts it: file_anchor_symbol() (the make_file_id node) and enclosing_declared_symbol() (nearest declared ancestor of given node types, by position). Anchor order: function, else enclosing type, else file. Ruby and lua moved onto them.\nProduction-path tests: packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_package_level_call_anchor.py (sweep fixtures per language, red before; IN_NAMED controls; swift init and kotlin class property anchor on the type). test_kotlin.py's test_call_at_top_level_outside_function_no_edge pinned the drop as a design choice and was rewritten.\nA/B, 0 lost everywhere: netavark +2, hummingbird +281 (struct 162, class 23, enum 1, file 95), sherpa-onnx +458 (class 406, object 9, file 43), lila +7,325 (class 4,052, object 2,176, file 988, trait 87, enum 22). Recorded aardvark-dns: +11 stub calls from const initialisers, each read back as a real call.\nResidual filed: WI-sogof (swift emits no symbol for init)."  # 6a0c
