  message: "PROGRESS 2026-09-26: JAVA, C, CPP DONE in PR #1237 (merged). Remaining: csharp (next PR) and WI-dokib (elixir's twin, own item). Status stays violated until csharp lands.\n\njava: method, else the enclosing class/interface/enum/record (by its own position index), else the file. c: function, else file only when inside NO function_definition. cpp: the walk starts at the file anchor and entering a function_definition resets it; the stack-construction arm stays function-only.\nTHE FIRST CUT OVER-REACHED and the read-back caught it: seeding the file anchor everywhere attributed calls inside UNNAMED functions to the file (cpp 81/166, c 12/18) and let the construction arm read extern declarations and member prototypes as constructions; GNU __attribute__ arguments and #if predicates parse as calls. All three are excluded, each pinned by a test that goes red without its guard. The unnamed-function gap is filed as WI-saduj.\nA/B, 0 lost: sherpa-onnx java +84 (class-anchored field initialisers), cpp +44 (file-scope MFC macros / ON_BN_CLICKED refs), crun c +3."  # 9402
