  message: "SATISFIED for the filed instance across all nine languages plus the csharp defect: PRs #1234 (ruby, lua), #1235 (rust, swift, kotlin, scala), #1237 (java, c, cpp), #1238 (csharp).\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE, this item's own sweep re-run on merged dev dbec60fb68 (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bamij_09262026/sweep_after.txt; before: every package-level line NONE, csharp calls=0):\n  rust     PKG_LITERAL -> file            | IN_NAMED -> named:function\n  java     PKG_LITERAL -> M:class, STATIC_INIT -> M:class | IN_NAMED -> M.named:method\n  kotlin   PKG_LITERAL, PKG_FIELD_LITERAL -> file | IN_NAMED -> named:function\n  swift    PKG_LITERAL -> file            | IN_NAMED -> named:function\n  ruby     PKG_LITERAL, PKG_FIELD_LITERAL -> file | IN_NAMED -> named:method\n  c        PKG_INIT_CALL -> file          | IN_NAMED -> named:function\n  cpp      PKG_INIT_CALL, PKG_LITERAL -> file | IN_NAMED -> named:function\n  csharp   PKG_LITERAL -> M:class         | IN_NAMED -> M.Named:method  (calls 0 -> 3)\n  scala    PKG_LITERAL -> M:object        | IN_NAMED -> M.named:method\n  lua      PKG_LITERAL, PKG_FIELD_LITERAL -> file | IN_NAMED -> named:function\nEvery IN_NAMED control keeps its named function (the item's \"NOT THIS ITEM\" line). Anchor rule, shared helpers in analyze/base.py: function, else enclosing type, else the file pseudo-symbol (make_file_id), the convention python/php already used.\n\nCorpus read-backs (0 edges lost anywhere): postal +105, kong +12,013, netavark +2, hummingbird +281, sherpa-onnx kotlin +458 / java +84 / cpp +44 / csharp +395, lila +7,325, crun +3.\n\nRESIDUALS, all filed: step 6 (DDG for these bodies) -> WI-nilir; c/cpp calls inside functions with no symbol -> WI-saduj; swift init has no symbol -> WI-sogof; ruby receiverless unresolved calls -> WI-napaf; ruby external-constant short-name binding -> WI-johib. WI-dokib (elixir, same shape) is its own item and is next."  # 2755
